A||N||3||dgroves||Car won't idle||||9||
Z||000000||dgroves||12-15-2001||01:53 PM||||Have just re assembled my 2.8. It's now a 3.1. Motor starts but will not keep running unless I blip the throttle. If I try to hold the RPM constant, it will die. If I let off the gas it will die. IAC valve is first to check. Any other ideas? Anybody had this problem?||||reg||9
Z||000001||avengador1||12-15-2001||05:16 PM||||What rpm's does it try to idle at? If the rpm's are too low you could adjust the idle stop screw. It's under a cover that has to be removed before you can get access on the throttle body. This might help.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Also, did you clean the IAC passages and the pintle seat while you rebuilt the engine?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||dgroves||12-15-2001||05:36 PM||||Nevermind.... I don't believe this myself but I went back to the car and it started and ran like there was nothing wrong. I adjusted the timing and it's like it was never apart. Must have been the ECM "Learning." Does that make sense?||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||12-15-2001||05:42 PM||||Yes, you should drive it normally  for about half an hour so the ECM can learn. Glad you figured it out yourself. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
